docs.remarks:
The scene belongs to the main thread. Worker threads are for pure computation: read what you need on the main thread, compute on a worker, then come back to apply the result.

```csharp
var input = BuildInput();
await GameTask.WorkerThread();
var result = Compute(input);
await GameTask.MainThread();
Apply(result);
```

Awaiting in a component resumes on the main thread already. When play stops or scripts reload, the session ends: [`SessionToken`](#api~Prowl.Runtime.GameTask~SessionToken) is cancelled and pending continuations are dropped, including a worker's hop back to the main thread when the work was started by gameplay code. Frame waits from an ended session complete as cancelled. Once the loop stops, requests for the main thread are refused.

When no engine loop is running, such as in a test or a tool, every thread counts as the main thread.
